        <Text>Research Question 2 (RQ2): Has the statistical relationship between a player’s height and their defensive position changed over the last 100 years? 
Hypothesis 2 (H2): The team believes there is a strong likelihood that a player’s height and the defensive position played has changed within the last 100 years. The variables causing this change is because of increased knowledge of general and sports medical care, increase supply of food to young children, resulting in children growing up taller, and a realization by baseball managers that certain positions are played better by players of certain heights.
</Text>
